<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulf of Taranto</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gulf of Tarentum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulf of Taranto is a gulf of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, between the heel and toe of the peninsula. In the 8th and 7th centuries BCE Greek colonists founded cities on its shores, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarentum">Taras</a> (Taranto), Metapontum, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sybaris">Sybaris</a> and Croton, which formed part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-graecia">Magna Graecia</a>. Taras had the best harbour on the gulf.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulf-of-taranto.jpg" alt="Gulf of Taranto" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yellow.Cat from Roma, Italy · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coastal_panorama_(4751155837).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
